{"id":"4b2d6446f806fb29f9bd55b157d99b6331d12bed","axis":"silent","repo":"webpack/webpack","sha":"4b2d6446f806fb29f9bd55b157d99b6331d12bed","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/070-shorter-runtime-code.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"webpack\": patch","+---","+","+Emit shorter runtime code for chunk loading, CSS, interop and module federation."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"AGENTS.md","lines":["@@ -246,6 +246,17 @@ CI's `lint` job verifies these are current; `yarn fix` (`fix:code` + `fix:specia"," "," Runtime-emitting code (chunk loading, resource hints, library and externals presets) is **per-target**: apply a change to **every** affected target with an integration case per target, then check wire cost with `yarn test:size` and say in the PR what moved. Targets, the universal runtime's DOM guard and how to read the size report: [docs/runtime.md](docs/runtime.md)."," ","+### Keep emitted runtime small","+","+> [!REQUIRED]","+","+**Emitted runtime is paid for in every user's bundle, so emit the shortest equivalent.** Read the checklist in [docs/runtime.md](docs/runtime.md#keep-emitted-runtime-small) before writing or changing an emitted string; the rules it enforces:","+","+- **Never hand-write a form a `RuntimeTemplate` helper covers** (`function(`, `var`, `x = x || y`, `hasOwnProperty.call`, `a && a.b`): the helper picks the shortest form per `output.environment`.","+- **Minifiers can't do it for you**: unused parameters, guards on values already known to be set, repeated property chains and default arguments survive terser.","+- **Emit only what this config runs**: gate code a feature, HMR or the import's usage needs behind that condition.","+- **Equivalence covers falsy values, prototype keys, the ES5 fallback and third-party overrides**; keep a guard you can't prove dead.","+"," ### Lint covers every file, docs included"," "," `lint` runs Prettier (`fmt:check`) and cspell (`lint:spellcheck`) over the **whole repo**, Markdown and this guide included. Run `yarn fix` before pushing even a docs change: an unaligned Markdown table or unknown word fails `lint` alone. Add a genuine new word to `words` in `cspell.json` (or reword); Prettier reformats Markdown tables, so hand-written columns must match its output."],"additions":11,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/runtime.md","lines":["@@ -5,3 +5,39 @@"," Runtime-emitting code — chunk loading (`lib/web/` JSONP, `lib/esm/`, `lib/node/`, `lib/webworker/`), prefetch/preload/resource hints, library and externals presets — is **per-target**: browsers/JSONP, ESM `output.module`, `node`, `webworker`, `deno`, `electron`, `bun`, and the **universal** `target: \"universal\"` / `[\"web\", \"node\"]` neutral-platform path each have their own module or wiring — changing one and forgetting the others is the easy mistake. Apply a change to **every** affected target, with an integration case per target (typically `target: \"web\"`, `output.module`, `target: \"universal\"` or `[\"web\", \"node\"]`; plus `node`/`webworker`/`bun`/`deno`/`electron` when in scope). The universal runtime guards browser APIs behind `typeof document === \"undefined\"` so its bundles run in Node without a DOM, and its config case must gate DOM assertions on `typeof document !== \"undefined\"` (see `configCases/target/universal-prefetch-preload`)."," "," **Then check wire cost** with `yarn test:size` (and the `Code Size` CI job, which comments the diff on the PR). It is information, never a verdict; how to read its report: [docs/performance.md](performance.md#reading-the-code-size-report). When the numbers moved, say what it reported in the PR.","+","+## Keep emitted runtime small","+","+Every byte a runtime module emits ships in every user's bundle that needs it, and a minifier can't recover most of the waste. Before writing or changing an emitted string, go through this list, then run `yarn test:size` and report the change in the PR.","+","+**Use the `RuntimeTemplate` helper, never a hand-written form it covers.** Each one picks the shortest form `output.environment` allows and keeps the ES5 fallback:","+","+| Hand-written                                    | Helper                                       |","+| ----------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |","+| `function(a, b) { … }`                          | `basicFunction`, `returningFunction`         |","+| `function() {}`                                 | `emptyFunction`                              |","+| `var x = …`                                     | `renderConst()`, `renderLet()`               |","+| `x = x \\|\\| y`, `if (x === undefined) x = y`    | `assignOr(\"x\", \"y\")` (when `\"\"`/`0` is safe) |","+| `a && a.b`                                      | `optionalChaining(\"a\", \"b\")`                 |","+| `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(o, k)`    | `objectHasOwn(\"o\", \"k\")`                     |","+| `var a = arr[0], b = arr[1]`                    | `destructureArray`, `destructureObject`      |","+| `\"a\" + b + \"c\"`                                 | `concatenation`                              |","+| `for (var i = 0; i < a.length; i++) { … a[i] }` | `forEach`                                    |","+| `name: function () { … }` inside an object      | `method`                                     |","+","+**Write what terser can't shorten.** It keeps unused parameters, property names and string keys, repeated `__webpack_require__.x` chains, default arguments such as `.bind(null, void 0, …)`, default descriptor fields (`configurable: false`) and guards on values the code already relies on:","+","+```diff","+ // `event` is dereferenced one line earlier, so the guard is dead","+-var errorType = event && event.type;","++var errorType = event.type;","+```","+","+**Emit only what this config runs.** Gate code behind the condition that needs it (HMR, a feature flag, whether any import reads the value), rather than emitting it for every build and relying on the minifier to drop it.","+","+**Prove equivalence before shortening.** Check every value the expression can hold:","+","+- Falsy values: `||` overwrites `0`, `\"\"` and `false`, so `assignOr` is only safe when those can't occur or rewriting them changes nothing.","+- Prototype keys: a chunk or module id such as `constructor` reads `Object.prototype`, so keep `hasOwnProperty` guards on id-keyed objects.","+- The ES5 fallback, for every helper whose modern form you measured.","+- Third-party overrides: a plugin or user can replace `__webpack_require__.*` functions and hooks, so keep a guard whose input comes from outside webpack unless you can prove it's dead."],"additions":36,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"lib/container/RemoteRuntimeModule.js","lines":["@@ -72,7 +72,6 @@ class RemoteRuntimeModule extends RuntimeModule {"," \t\t\t}"," \t\t}"," \t\tconst cst = runtimeTemplate.renderConst();","-\t\tconst lt = runtimeTemplate.renderLet();"," \t\treturn Template.asString(["," \t\t\t`${cst} chunkMapping = ${JSON.stringify("," \t\t\t\tchunkToRemotesMapping,","@@ -90,8 +89,7 @@ class RemoteRuntimeModule extends RuntimeModule {"," \t\t\t\t`if(${RuntimeGlobals.hasOwnProperty}(chunkMapping, chunkId)) {`,"," \t\t\t\tTemplate.indent(["," \t\t\t\t\t`chunkMapping[chunkId].forEach(${runtimeTemplate.basicFunction(\"id\", [","-\t\t\t\t\t\t`${lt} getScope = ${RuntimeGlobals.currentRemoteGetScope};`,","-\t\t\t\t\t\t\"if(!getScope) getScope = [];\",","+\t\t\t\t\t\t`${cst} getScope = ${RuntimeGlobals.currentRemoteGetScope} || [];`,"," \t\t\t\t\t\t`${cst} data = idToExternalAndNameMapping[id];`,"," \t\t\t\t\t\t\"if(getScope.indexOf(data) >= 0) return;\","," \t\t\t\t\t\t\"getScope.push(data);\","],"additions":1,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"lib/css/CssInjectStyleRuntimeModule.js","lines":["@@ -130,8 +130,7 @@ class CssInjectStyleRuntimeModule extends RuntimeModule {"," \t\t\t\t\tTemplate.indent(\"return el;\"),"," \t\t\t\